{"id":"hotchkiss-1915","title":"Effie and Avis Hotchkiss: coast to coast","who":"Effie Hotchkiss & her mother Avis","when":"1915","vehicle":"Harley-Davidson 11-F with sidecar","kind":"moto","color":"#9333ea","summary":"Effie Hotchkiss, 26, a Wall Street worker, rides her new three-speed Harley from Brooklyn to San Francisco with her 56-year-old mother Avis in the sidecar, doing her own repairs, to see the Panama-Pacific Exposition: the first women to cross the United States by motorcycle. At Ocean Beach they poured Atlantic water they had carried into the Pacific.","sources":[{"label":"Rider Magazine: Effie's great adventure","url":"https://ridermagazine.com/effies-great-adventure-first-women-to-ride-cross-country/"},{"label":"The Vintagent: first women motorcyclists across the USA","url":"https://thevintagent.com/?p=75295"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Avis and Effie Hotchkiss","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avis_and_Effie_Hotchkiss"}],"approximate":"Places named in accounts of the ride; the 1915 roads are drawn as today's, only approximately.","km":5037,"bbox":[-122.5089,37.7562,-73.7488,43.2488],"stops":[{"name":"Brooklyn","place":"Brooklyn, New York","at":[40.6526,-73.9497],"date":"2 May 1915","text":"Off with a jar of Atlantic water, tools and a gun.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Brooklyn_skyline.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_skyline.jpg","page":"Brooklyn","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brooklyn_skyline.jpg","credit":"Sashimi-b","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Albany","place":"Albany, New York","at":[42.6512,-73.755],"text":"Up the Hudson valley.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Albany%2C_New_York.jpg/500px-Albany%2C_New_York.jpg","page":"Albany, New York","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albany%2C_New_York.jpg","credit":"Quintin Soloviev","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Buffalo","place":"Buffalo, New York","at":[42.8864,-78.8781],"text":"West along t